{"name":"Chickadee","hex":"#ffcf65","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chickadee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the small, mostly black and white North American songbirds of the genus Poecile of the family Paridae.","Affectionate term of address."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chickadee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chickadee (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Chickadee is a 2012 historical fiction novel by American author Louise Erdrich, the fourth book in The Birchbark House series. Moving the story fourteen years into the future, the novel follows Omakayas's twin sons, Chickadee and Makoons, as the family moves further into the Great Plains. When Chickadee is kidnapped, he embarks on a journey to reunite with his family against a backdrop of American westward expansion."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Front_cover_of_Chickadee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chickadee_(novel)"},{"title":"Chickadee (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Chickadee is a Canadian monthly children's magazine. It was founded in 1979 as a spin-off of OWL Magazine geared towards younger readers. Its headquarters is in Toronto."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b7/Chick_JanFeb12_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chickadee_(magazine)"},{"title":"Poecile","blocks":[{"text":"Poecile is a genus of birds in the tit family Paridae. It contains 15 species, which are distributed across Europe, Asia, and North America; the European and Asian species are known as tits, and the North American species as chickadees. In the past, most authorities retained Poecile as a subgenus within the genus Parus, but treatment as a distinct genus, initiated by the American Ornithologists Union, is now widely accepted. This is supported by mtDNA cytochrome b sequence analysis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Sumpfmeise.jpg/330px-Sumpfmeise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poecile"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg/500px-Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg/1280px-Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg/500px-Chestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChestnut-backed_Chickadee_-_MGL0807.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/White-browed_tit_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-White-browed_tit_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/White-browed_tit_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-White-browed_tit_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite-browed_tit_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Poecile_lugubris%2C_Bulgaria_1.jpg/500px-Poecile_lugubris%2C_Bulgaria_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Poecile_lugubris%2C_Bulgaria_1.jpg/1280px-Poecile_lugubris%2C_Bulgaria_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w